course: dictionary
lesson: 13736
title: The word intensity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intensity means how strong or extreme something is. You can talk about the intensity of a storm, a sound or a feeling. More intensity means something is stronger.
explain: «The sun had high intensity at noon.» High intensity means very strong. «The rain fell with low intensity» means it was gentle. To check, swap strong or gentle into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In science, intensity can be measured. A light sensor shows the intensity of light, and sound intensity is measured in decibels. «She played with great intensity» means she put a lot of strong effort and feeling into the game.
fact: Intensity is a noun. Its plural is intensities.
fact: «Intensity» means how strong or extreme something is.
fact: In science, «intensity» can mean the amount of light, sound, heat or energy.
fact: Useful phrases: «high intensity», «low intensity» and «with intensity».
fact: «Intensity» can also mean strong feeling or seriousness, as in «He played with great intensity.»
exercise: «The storm had great intensity, and the wind shook the windows.» What does intensity mean here? | The name of the storm | How long the storm lasted | The colour of the clouds | *How strong the storm was
exercise: A science sensor measures the light intensity in the room. What is being measured? | *How strong the light is | What colour the walls are | How far away the window is | How many lamps there are
exercise: Which phrase means with strong, serious feeling? | Morning intensities | Light sensor | Low intensity | *With intensity
test: «She trained with great intensity every morning.» What does intensity mean? | A kind of morning | Going slowly | Feeling cold | *Strong effort and feeling
test: What does «high intensity» mean? | Very old | Very far away | Very quiet and gentle | *Very strong or extreme
exam: In science, sound intensity is measured in decibels. Which unit is used for sound intensity? | *Decibels | Kilograms | Metres | Litres
